{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 -c \\\"\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('update.json'))\nprint(list(d.keys()))\nprint(json.dumps(d, indent=1)[:3000])\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"['rationale', 'interpretations']\n{\n \"rationale\": \"Recorded the compatibility reasoning for the transfer account's two receipts, which its prose and executions map already relied on but which the record did not state: they come from the same harness and its revision, the revision having added only the 1ms leadership sampler and two comparisons for the non-voter case while leaving the cases, target selection and measured fields identical. The first receipt therefore carries the reported result and endpoint states and the second the leaderless interval. Nothing else in the account changed and no execution was requested.\",\n \"interpretations\": [\n  {\n   \"investigation_id\": \"627b3ef0c6e049bfb836e40ffbdce875-question-1\",\n   \"experiment_id\": null,\n   \"source_ids\": [\n    \"api_transfer_to_server\",\n    \"transfer_target_lookup\",\n    \"timeout_now\",\n    \"candidate_skips_prevote\",\n    \"vote_term_bump\",\n    \"transfer_lost_leadership\",\n    \"pick_server_voters\",\n    \"follower_vote_grant\",\n    \"docs_transfer\",\n    \"start_stop_repl\"\n   ],\n   \"executions\": {\n    \"b2c0026c56d54511999e5c37ef8372cd\": [\n     1,\n     3\n    ],\n    \"23acf06d8a524b2790ef674d5eb04cb0\": [\n     0,\n     1,\n     2,\n     3\n    ]\n   },\n   \"conclusion\": \"explained\",\n   \"defect_claim\": \"asserted\",\n   \"rationale\": \"The question was whether LeadershipTransferToServer reports a transfer that the named server can complete when that server is a non-voter, and what happens to leadership while it cannot; both halves are now execution-backed. Naming a voter (receipt 23acf06d8a524b2790ef674d5eb04cb0, setup index 0 and result index 1, and the earlier receipt b2c0026c56d54511999e5c37ef8372cd) the call returned nil, the requested server was Leader at the endpoint and the previous leader Follower, so the call does perform real transfers. Naming the non-voter (setup index 2, result index 3) the same call returned nil while the requested server was never observed as Leader and finished Follower; the previous leader was outside Leader state in all 1289 samples taken from the instant of the call; 241 samples found no leader in the cluster at all, the first 1ms and the last 278ms after the call, so the cluster was leaderless for about 277ms against a 200ms election timeout; the maximum term rose from 2 to 4; and leadership ended on a voter other than the requested target. The source explains the mechanism as predicted. The leader resolves the requested ID only through leaderState.replState, which startStopReplication populates for every configured server except the leader without consulting Suffrage, so a non-voter passes and receives TimeoutNow; timeoutNow sets it to Candidate and marks candidateFromLeadershipTransfer, a flag that by design suppresses pre-vote, so it sends a real RequestVote carrying the next term. Every voter adopts the higher term and becomes a follower before reaching the hasVote check, which then refuses the vote because the candidate holds no vote, so the requested server can never collect a grant. The old leader learns of the h\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
